{# The 401 body from ``POST /account/logout``. You only get to read this
   after cancelling the browser's password prompt — the prompt IS the
   sign-out (see precis_web.routes.account.logout), so this page explains
   the thing that just happened rather than claiming to have done it. #}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Signed out{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h1 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">Signed out</h1>
<p class="text-sm text-fg-subtle mb-5 max-w-2xl">
  Your browser was asked to forget the password it was holding
  {%- if user %} for <code class="text-fg-muted">{{ user.login }}</code>{% endif %}.
</p>

<div class="rounded-lg border border-warning bg-warning-subtle px-4 py-3 text-sm
            text-warning-deep max-w-2xl mb-5">
  <strong>If the browser is asking for a password right now, cancel it.</strong>
  That prompt is the sign-out. Typing the password back in signs you straight
  back in, which is also a perfectly good way to leave.
</div>

<p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle max-w-2xl mb-3">
  HTTP Basic has no session for a server to end: the credential lives in the
  browser and is re-sent on every request until the browser decides to drop it.
  All this page can do is answer with a challenge it can't satisfy — every
  mainstream browser responds by discarding what it had. On a shared or
  borrowed machine, quit the browser: that is the only guarantee, and it is a
  property of Basic auth, not of this server.
</p>

<p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle max-w-2xl">
  <a href="/account" class="text-info-strong hover:underline">Sign back in</a>
  — any page will prompt.
</p>
{% endblock %}
